  "schema_version": 1,
  "title": "Chapter 5 tutorial — Care to Compare (combined CARE)",
  "created": "2026-09-02T08:43:01+00:00",
  "modified": "2026-09-02T08:43:01+00:00",
  "notes": "Worked example of how Chapter 5 maps onto the four-stage evaluation framework. The data source is the open Care to Compare (C2C) benchmark (Gück et al., 2024), farms A and B, generator-bearing and rotor-bearing cases. Chapter 5 also constructed Kelmarsh and Penmanshiel cases; those are omitted here so one open source can be followed end-to-end.\n\nThe method is an NBM residual Monitoring Indicator (FFNN, LSTM or TCN) and, as a separate comparator, direct AD on the raw target temperature. Five AD Algorithms (SCC, EWMA-CC, CUSUM, KSCAD, BCAD) produce instance-level alarms. Combined detection performance is CARE (Coverage, Accuracy, Reliability, Earliness).\n\nOpen this .fddx in FDD Evaluation and click through Inputs and Stages 1–4. This file is a protocol example, not a scored result table.",
  "inputs": {
    "data_types": [
      "data_scada",
      "data_alarms"
    ],
    "records": [
      "rec_operator",
      "rec_expert",
      "rec_logbook",
      "rec_service"
    ],
    "cost_inputs": [],
    "method": "method_nbm",
    "method_notes": "Decoupled NBM–AD pipeline from Chapter 5. An NBM (FFNN, LSTM or TCN) is trained on the healthy training period of each case to estimate the target bearing temperature. The residual is the Monitoring Indicator for residual-based AD. Direct AD on the raw target temperature is retained as a second Monitoring Indicator so residual monitoring can be compared with AD on the measured series. AD Algorithms: SCC, EWMA-CC, CUSUM, KSCAD and BCAD. Each AD Algorithm is fitted on the healthy training period and applied to the test period, producing a binary alarm sequence a_t."
  },
  "stage1": {
    "primary_objective": "obj_early_warning",
    "secondary_objectives": [],
    "early_warning": {
      "reference_event": "Recorded C2C fault event that ends the expert-defined pre-fault event window (component fault associated with generator-bearing or rotor-bearing temperature).",
      "detection_point": "detect_fd_condition",
      "notes": "Early Warning: obtain sufficient anomaly evidence before the recorded fault while remaining stable on matched healthy cases. Lead time is taken from the first time the case-level fault-detection condition is satisfied, not from the first isolated detected anomaly. CARE Earliness still rewards earlier instance-level evidence inside the event window."
    },
